ITEMS=[]
def family(options,rows):
 for k,(stem,why) in enumerate(rows):ITEMS.append((stem,[options[k]]+options[:k]+options[k+1:],why))
family(['A boom-angle indicator','An anti-two-block device','A drum-rotation indicator','A load-weighing device'],[
('Which aid tells the operator the boom’s inclination rather than the load’s weight?','A boom-angle indicator shows boom inclination; it does not establish load weight.'),
('Which device addresses dangerous contact between the lower load block and the boom-tip assembly?','An anti-two-block device addresses contact between the lower block/ball and the boom tip or upper block.'),
('Which aid helps an operator detect motion of a hoist drum that cannot be seen directly?','A drum-rotation indicator reports drum movement; it is not a load-moment limiter.'),
('Which aid directly indicates the weight being supported rather than boom geometry or drum movement?','A load-weighing device indicates load weight, subject to its proper setup and limitations.')])
family(['A working crane-level indicator','A working horn within reach','An integral jack holding valve','A lock on the foot-pedal brake'],[
('Which safety device provides the operator with information needed to check whether the machine is level?','OSHA1926.1415 requires a crane-level indicator on covered equipment, with specified exceptions.'),
('Which safety device provides an immediately available audible warning to people around the crane?','A horn must be built in or immediately available to the operator under1926.1415.'),
('Which required hydraulic-outrigger feature helps retain the jack’s support against unintended hydraulic movement?','Hydraulic outrigger and stabilizer jacks require an integral holding device/check valve.'),
('Which required device keeps an equipped foot-pedal brake in its selected holding position?','Equipment with foot-pedal brakes must have locks under1926.1415.')])
family(['Stop until communication returns','Agree on the signals beforehand','Use the operator’s perspective','Identify the crane being addressed'],[
('A blind lift depends on radio signals, and the radio link suddenly fails. What is the required response?','Safely stop operations requiring signals until communication is reestablished and a proper signal is understood.'),
('A special attachment cannot be directed with the standard hand-signal method. What must the operator, signal person and lift director do before using non-standard hand signals?','They must agree on the non-standard signals before the operation under1926.1419(c)(2).'),
('A signal person faces the operator from the opposite side of the load. From whose viewpoint must left/right directions be expressed?','All directions must use the operator’s perspective, avoiding reversed interpretations.'),
('One signal person communicates with two cranes on a coordination channel. What must make each instruction’s intended recipient clear?','The crane must be identified before function/direction or through an equally effective identification method.')])
family(['Test the radio system on site','Receive through a hands-free system','Use a dedicated signal channel','Confirm a shared working language'],[
('Before a radio-controlled lift begins, what checks that signal transmission is clear, effective and reliable at that site?','The transmitting devices must be tested on site before operations under1926.1420(a).'),
('Which reception arrangement lets the operator hear transmitted instructions without holding a communication device?','OSHA1926.1420(c) requires hands-free reception by the operator.'),
('Ordinary unrelated radio traffic is interfering with lift instructions. Which channel arrangement does OSHA generally require, subject to its stated coordination exceptions?','Signal transmission generally uses a dedicated channel, with specified exceptions for coordinated operations.'),
('The operator and signal person use different spoken languages. What must be established for voice signals to be effective?','The operator, signal person and lift director must be able to communicate effectively in the language used.')])
family(['A qualified plan developer','The designated lift director','The utility owner/operator','Any person noticing the hazard'],[
('Before two cranes support one load, who must develop the lift plan?','A qualified person develops the multiple-crane lift plan under1926.1432(a).'),
('Who must review a multiple-crane lift plan in a meeting with all workers involved before implementing the lift?','The lift director reviews the plan with the involved workers under1926.1432(b).'),
('For a power-line plan using Table A, who provides the requested line-voltage information?','The utility owner/operator provides voltage information under1926.1408(c).'),
('A worker other than the designated signal person sees someone enter immediate danger. Who may give the emergency-stop signal?','Anyone aware of a safety problem may give the stop or emergency-stop signal, which the operator must obey.')])
family(['Verify the load by reliable data','Check seating of slack rope','Confirm controls and people clear','Use the specified counterweight'],[
('A load-indicating method shows that a load exceeds75% of maximum rated capacity at the longest planned radius. What must happen before proceeding under OSHA1926.1417(o)(3)?','Weight must be verified by an industry-recognised source, calculation or equally reliable means before proceeding.'),
('A competent person identifies slack rope that requires re-spooling. What must be verified as slack is removed before lifting?','The rope must be correctly seated on the drum and in the sheaves under1926.1417(m).'),
('Immediately before starting the engine, what operational check does OSHA require?','The operator verifies proper starting positions of controls and that personnel are clear.'),
('The setup requires ballast, and spare ballast is available nearby. What must determine the amount installed?','The manufacturer-specified counterweight/ballast must be installed; the specified maximum must not be exceeded.')])
family(['Stop and restore the safety device','Use the specified temporary measure','Restore access to rated capacities','Report repairs promptly in writing'],[
('A required horn stops working, and no other compliant horn is immediately available. What must happen before crane operation resumes?','A required safety device must be restored to proper operation;1926.1415 does not permit alternative measures.'),
('A listed operational aid fails. Its OSHA provision permits a specific temporary alternative during repair, and any more protective manufacturer measures are met. What allows operation after a safe stop?','The specified temporary alternative may be implemented during the allowed repair period; this does not apply to safety-device failures.'),
('The only load chart in the cab is electronic, and its display fails. Which condition must be restored after safely stopping?','Rated capacities must again be accessible, electronically or otherwise, before operations resume.'),
('An operator determines that equipment adjustments or repairs are necessary. What communication is required to the employer’s designated recipient and next operator on successive shifts?','The operator must promptly inform those persons in writing under1926.1417(j).')])
family(['A nonconductive tag line','A verified load-weight record','A manufacturer travel procedure','A controlled swing speed'],[
('A tag line is needed within a power-line encroachment-control plan. What type is required?','Tag lines used under1926.1408(b) must be nonconductive; this does not remove other electrical precautions.'),
('A supplier’s equipment package has no marked weight. Which information is needed to establish the load’s mass before lifting by a reliable-source method?','A manufacturer record or other equally reliable load-weight information supports capacity verification.'),
('A crew proposes moving the crane with a suspended load. Which equipment-specific instruction must be checked for a prohibition on that practice?','Travel with a load is prohibited if the manufacturer prohibits it; additional supervised travel requirements also apply.'),
('A suspended load starts swinging outward as the upperworks rotate. Which operating variable must be limited to keep the load within a controllable radius?','Rotational speed must keep the load from swinging beyond a radius at which it can be controlled.')])
family(['Wind, ice and snow effects','Tire inflation and condition','Boom clearance from obstructions','Hazardous load rotation'],[
('A competent person reassesses equipment stability and rated capacity as weather worsens. Which conditions is OSHA1926.1417(n) specifically addressing?','Wind, ice and snow can affect stability and rated capacity and require appropriate adjustment.'),
('A wheeled crane is permitted to travel with a load. Which wheel-related condition must meet manufacturer specifications?','The specified tire pressure must be maintained; tire condition also belongs in shift inspections.'),
('The intended swing path brings the boom beside a building projection. Which condition must remain satisfied throughout movement?','The boom and other equipment must not contact obstructions under1926.1417(p).'),
('A long suspended assembly can turn and strike workers. What condition makes a tag or restraint line necessary under the operating rule?','A tag/restraint line is required when necessary to prevent hazardous rotation of the load.')])
family(['Stop the affected movement safely','Continue the agreed clear movement','Reassess before the changed movement','Secure before leaving unattended'],[
('A valid emergency-stop signal is given during hoisting. What is the operator’s response?','A stop or emergency-stop signal must be obeyed; safely stop the affected operation.'),
('The planned movement remains within the verified capacity and clearances, communication is reliable, no safety problem exists, and the designated signal person gives the agreed hoist signal. What is appropriate?','With all stated conditions satisfied, perform the authorised controlled movement; an unnecessary stop is not required by the scenario.'),
('A load’s destination changes to a greater radius that has not been checked against the chart. What must happen before that new movement?','The new radius and configuration must be evaluated against rated capacity before making the changed movement.'),
('The load has been landed and the shift is ending. What must the operator do before leaving the crane unattended?','Follow manufacturer shutdown and securing procedures; merely landing the load does not complete shutdown.')])
family(['8,000 pounds','9,000 pounds','10,000 pounds','12,000 pounds'],[
('For a stated reeving plan, four supporting parts are each allowed2,000lb and the plan ignores efficiency losses. What is the line-limited load, before checking other crane limits?','4×2,000=8,000lb. Actual reeving information and all crane limits still govern.'),
('An operator will handle a load at90% of a stated10,000lb maximum line pull. What line force marks that90% threshold?','0.90×10,000=9,000lb; the OSHA brake-test threshold refers to maximum line pull, not chart capacity.'),
('A documented load consists of an8,500lb component plus1,500lb of included contents. What total load weight must be considered before adding separate lifting gear?','8,500+1,500=10,000lb; separate gear deductions or additions still follow the chart notes.'),
('A verified16,000lb maximum rated capacity applies at the longest radius. What is75% of that capacity for the OSHA load-weight verification threshold?','0.75×16,000=12,000lb; exceeding that threshold under the indicating-device method requires reliable weight verification.')])
family(['Measure the boom angle or radius','Measure or mark the boom length','Verify the outrigger positions','Mark and view the hoist drum'],[
('A required boom-angle/radius indicator fails during repair. What specified temporary method determines the geometry?','Measure the radius or boom angle with a measuring device under1926.1416(e)(1).'),
('A telescopic boom-length indicator fails. Which listed temporary method directly establishes boom length?','Measured marks or direct measurement are among the permitted alternatives under1926.1416(e)(3).'),
('An outrigger-extension monitor fails during repair. What must the operator verify before operations requiring outrigger deployment?','The actual outrigger/stabilizer position must be verified as correct under manufacturer procedures.'),
('An out-of-view hoist drum’s rotation indicator fails. What listed temporary measure allows drum movement to be observed?','Mark the drum and provide mirrors or video if necessary so the operator can see the mark under1926.1416(e)(5).')])
family(['Before the first heavy duty-cycle lift','Before relying on the boom brake','After resolving the signal problem','Before changing the voice signals'],[
('Repetitive duty-cycle lifts each exceed90% of maximum line pull. When does the OSHA few-inches lift-and-brake test apply within that repetitive sequence?','For duty-cycle/repetitive lifts at that threshold, the test applies to the first lift, not every successive lift.'),
('During assembly, the crew plans to rely on the boom-hoist brake to prevent movement. When must that brake’s ability to hold be tested?','The brake must be tested before reliance is placed on it under1926.1404(h)(10).'),
('The operator has stopped after discovering a safety problem that must be discussed with the signal person. When may the operation resume?','Both must agree the problem has been resolved before operations resume under1926.1419(g).'),
('A crew proposes using a different set of voice commands halfway through a job. When must the operator, signal person and lift director agree on the revised commands?','They must agree before using changed voice signals; the earlier agreement does not cover the change.')])
family(['Increased load radius','Reduced buoyant support','A sudden dynamic force','A lateral boom force'],[
('A loaded boom bends downward and its tip moves farther horizontally from the axis of rotation. Which chart-related change must be considered?','The load radius increases; capacity must be assessed at the actual loaded geometry.'),
('A submerged object is lifted until it emerges from the water. Which change can increase the force carried by the crane?','Buoyant support decreases as the object leaves the water, increasing the supported load.'),
('A moving suspended load is arrested abruptly instead of smoothly. Which effect can increase forces beyond the static load?','Abrupt acceleration or stopping introduces dynamic force, commonly called shock loading.'),
('A crew tries to drag a load sideways with the hoist line instead of lifting vertically. Which force is imposed on the boom?','Side pulling imposes lateral loading; OSHA1926.1417(q) prohibits dragging or pulling loads sideways.')])
assert len(ITEMS)==56
